iommu: apple-dart: raise MAX_DARTS_PER_DEVICE to 8

The display-subsystem lists one scanout DART (stream 0) per DCP. Wiring all
four M2 Max external DCPs (dcpext0..3) plus disp0 needs five; the stock cap
of 3 makes apple_dart_of_xlate() reject the extras with -EINVAL, so dcpext2/3
get no scanout mapping and the DCP firmware faults on the first frame.

--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@
 
 #define DART_MAX_STREAMS 256
 #define DART_MAX_TTBR 4
-#define MAX_DARTS_PER_DEVICE 3
+#define MAX_DARTS_PER_DEVICE 8
 #define DART_PCIEC_PAGE_SHIFT 14
 #define DART_PCIEC_ADDR_WIDTH 42
 #define DART_PCIEC_STREAMS 64
